# Chromium command line (read from /data/local/tmp on debuggable builds) for the software
# Vulkan driver (pastel, the real PC's ro.hardware.vulkan): Chromium's GPU process
# otherwise draws with Skia Graphite on Dawn/Vulkan, whose vkGetSemaphoreFdKHR fails there,
# so the GPU process crashes and restarts over and over and the window flickers black.
# Ganesh (Skia's GL backend) on the system EGL (ANGLE) works; VulkanFromANGLE must go too,
# and Vulkan itself must stay enabled, or the GPU process is declared unusable and the
# browser exits (tried in QEMU with the same images).
# Installed on /product so it runs in init's domain (vendor_init may not write
# /data/local/tmp).
on property:sys.boot_completed=1 && property:ro.hardware.vulkan=pastel
    write /data/local/tmp/chrome-command-line "_ --disable-features=SkiaGraphite,VulkanFromANGLE"
    chmod 0644 /data/local/tmp/chrome-command-line

# G4 (docs/nvidia.md): on the NVK entry ANGLE runs on the RTX 4070, and Chromium keeps the
# same path: Ganesh on the system EGL (ANGLE on NVK), so its GPU process draws on the GPU.
# Dawn/Graphite on NVK is untried; the same flags keep the one route that works on both
# entries. The file stays on /data across entries, so each entry writes its own.
on property:sys.boot_completed=1 && property:ro.hardware.vulkan=nouveau
    write /data/local/tmp/chrome-command-line "_ --disable-features=SkiaGraphite,VulkanFromANGLE"
    chmod 0644 /data/local/tmp/chrome-command-line
